  "interpretation": [
    "QoS 0 slow-subscriber drop counters exactly matched missing delivery counts.",
    "QoS 2 lost 570 subscriber deliveries under overload even though publisher completion handshakes finished; logs recorded client store quota reached (MaximumInflight=8192). The cluster forwarding and $SYS messages/dropped counters did not capture this quota loss.",
    "QoS 1 had no missing messages in any tested workload; it slowed senders and accumulated latency/backlog. The 100k/s 30-second run required an additional 2.67 seconds to finish deliveries.",
    "CONNECT refusal bursts during churn returned 0x88 and matched broker claim failures. No SUBACK rejection occurred for successfully connected clients. A repeated 128-worker run passed, so concurrency 128 is not a deterministic capacity threshold.",
    "All rates describe this shared 14-vCPU Docker Desktop VM with an in-cluster generator, plaintext MQTT and the local allow-all profile. They are workload-specific observations, not universal broker capacity guarantees.",
    "Latency is sampled and includes publisher-side waiting and subscriber processing. Kubelet resource samples are coarse and can lag the workload."
  ]
